-- title:
--   Reduction kernel at the node is the branch ideal (varpi, j_q-j^{ q})
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ a ring homomorphism; let $a\in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2}=a$, and let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with $A_0=\mathrm{coeffSubring}\,A\,K=A\cap K$ and $\mathrm{redRestrict}\,\mathrm{red}\,K$ the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to $A_0$. Assume $\varpi\in A_0$ generates the kernel of this restriction, in the sense that for all $c\in A_0$ one has $\mathrm{redRestrict}\,\mathrm{red}\,K\,c=0$ exactly when $c=\varpi d$ for some $d\in A_0$. Let $g$ belong to $\mathrm{modularLocalizedAtPoint}$ at level $1\cdot q$ for $A_0$ at the point $(a,a^q)$, i.e. the subring of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting of those $f$ with $f\cdot\mathrm{modularEval}(s)=\mathrm{modularEval}(r)$ for some $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ whose value $\mathrm{pointEval}$ at $(a,a^q)$, coefficients reduced, satisfies $s(a,a^q)\neq 0$; here $\mathrm{modularEval}$ evaluates $X_0\mapsto jqModC$, $X_1\mapsto jqNModC$ at level $1\cdot q$ with coefficients sent to constant series. Assume moreover that $g$, as a Laurent series, lies in $\mathrm{CharPReduction.modularLocalized}$ at level $1\cdot q$ for $A$ and $\mathrm{red}$, the localisation of the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ together with $jqModC$ and $jqNModC$ at the complement of its reduction-kernel prime. Then the coefficientwise reduction $\mathrm{modularRedLocHom}$ of $g$ in the Laurent series over $k$ vanishes if and only if $g$ lies in the ideal of $\mathrm{modularLocalizedAtPoint}$ generated by the two elements $\mathrm{modularEval}(C\,\varpi)$ and $\mathrm{modularEval}(X_1-X_0^{\,q})$.
--
--   This identifies the kernel of the reduction of Gauss-integral $\mathfrak q$-expansions on the local ring of the plane model of $X_0(q)$ at the point $(a,a^q)$ of its special fibre as the branch ideal $(\varpi,\;j_q-j^{\,q})$, the prime cutting out the component through the cusp $\infty$, on which $j_q=j^{\,q}$ in characteristic $q$. It is used by the lemmas producing Gauss coordinates and crossing presentations at such points, including the normal forms at the points above $j=0$ and $j=1728$.
-- source:
